   "source": [
    "1] Understanding of problem statement\n",
    "2] Data Ingestion\n",
    "3] Data prepration / Preprocessing\n",
    "        --> Missing Value treatment\n",
    "        --> Class Imbalance\n",
    "        --> Outlier treatment\n",
    "        --> Data Encoding\n",
    "        --> Feature engineering /  Feature Extraction"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "id": "3635348e-d0b8-47a5-847b-a3a639db4974",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    " --------------->>>>>>Feature Extraction -->\n",
    "    --> Creating new feature\n",
    "    --> modifying the exist feature\n",
    "    --> Selecting the right feature\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "Feature Extraction --> Process of Selecting And Extracting the Relevant feaatures from the raw Data\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "All The Features Can not be relevant for machine learning models\n",
    "-->How It can be Problem?\n",
    "    --> Here Comes a Concept Called as CURSE OF DIMENSIONALITY\n",
    "        -> With Increase in number of Features :-\n",
    "            1] Model traning becomes computationally expensive\n",
    "            2] Model interpretation becomes complex\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "How To Solve ?\n",
    "-> 1] Creating new Features \n",
    "        1] Example: Health Data\n",
    "        📌 Given Data:\n",
    "        Weight = 70 kg\n",
    "        Height = 1.75 m\n",
    "        ⚙️ New Feature Created:\n",
    "        BMI = Weight / Height² = 22.86  # New Feature Created Instead of 2 Feature you using Single Feature\n",
    "\n",
    "        \n",
    "        👉 Used to classify health condition.\n",
    "\n",
    "        2]Example: House Price Prediction\n",
    "            📌 Given Data:\n",
    "            Total Price = ₹50,00,000\n",
    "            Area = 1000 sq.ft\n",
    "            ⚙️ New Feature Created:\n",
    "            Price per sq.ft = 5000000 / 1000 = ₹5000\n",
    "            \n",
    "            👉 Helps compare properties.\n",
    "\n"
   ]
  },
